<title>JAPAN: Nippon Oil, Cosmo to buy term condensate from ADNOC.</title>
<headline>Nippon Oil, Cosmo to buy term condensate from ADNOC.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Oil Co Ltd and Cosmo Oil Co Ltd will start importing condensate from Abu Dhabi National Oil Co (ADNOC) on a term basis starting in July, traders with the Japanese oil firms said on Monday.</p>
<p>Cosmo plans to import 5,500 barrels-per-day (bpd) and Nippon Oil 3,300 bpd of Thammama condensate, they said.</p>
<p>The condensate will be blended with crude oil and processed in crude distillation units mainly for naphtha production, they said.</p>
<p>The term price was unavailable, but some naphtha traders said it was likely to be set at a discount to ADNOC's official selling prices for Murban crude oil.</p>
<p>Condensate is a high quality oil with high product yields.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Energy Desk +81-3-3432-8837</p>
</text>
